title:: BMMIDIPort
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - represents a MIDI connection
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMMIDIPort represents a single MIDI connection.

See also: link::Classes/Controllers/BMAbstractMIDIController::, link::Classes/MIDI::, link::Classes/MIDIIn::, link::Classes/MIDIOut::

Section:: Double-sided vs. Single-sided Ports

When strong::*init:: is called it constructs an link::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: of all available ports. If a source has a matching destination this method will combine them into a single port, otherwise you can have ports with only a source or only a destination (i.e. only input or output).

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: init
This constructs the list of available ports, calling MIDIIn.connectAll if MIDIClient has not been initialized.


method:: new
Create a new BMMIDIPort. Normally you would not do this directly; rather it is done automatically when you call strong::*init::.

argument:: name
A String corresponding to the name of this port.
argument:: inuid
The inuid. This should be the same as the corresponding source MIDIEndPoint.
argument:: outuid
The outuid. This should be the same as the corresponding destination MIDIEndPoint.
argument:: device
A String corresponding to the name of this port's device. This should be the same as the corresponding source MIDIEndPoint(s).
argument:: outport
The index of this port's destination MIDIEndPoint in MIDIClient.destinations.


INSTANCEMETHODS::
	
method:: ports
If argument::*init:: has been called this will return an IdentityDictionary containing all available ports. Keys are Symbols corresponding to each port's name.
				
method:: initialised
Returns a link::Classes/Boolean:: indicating whether or not *init has been called.
	
method:: inuid
This port's inuid. This should be the same as the corresponding source MIDIEndPoint.
					
method:: outuid
This port's outuid. This should be the same as the corresponding destination MIDIEndPoint.
				
method:: device
Returns a link::Classes/String:: indicating the name of this port's device.
				
method:: outport
The index of this port's destination MIDIEndPoint in MIDIClient.destinations.
				
method:: name
Returns a link::Classes/Symbol:: indicating the name of this port.
				

method:: initFromArchive
Checks to see if *init has already been called, and if not, posts a warning.


Examples::

code::
// initialise
BMMIDIPort.init;

// all ports
p = BMMIDIPort.ports;
(
EZPopUpMenu.new(nil, items: p.keys.collectAs({|k| k->{|men| 
	("You selected " ++ p[men.widget.item]).postln; 
	NoteOnResponder({ |src,chan,note,vel|
		[src,chan,note,vel].postln;
	}, p[men.widget.item].inuid)	
}}, Array))
)
::
